Allocate Minimum Pages

Given an array arr[] of integers, where each element arr[i] represents the number 
of pages in the i-th book. You also have an integer k representing the number of students. 
The task is to allocate books to each student such that:

Each student receives atleast one book.
Each student is assigned a contiguous sequence of books.
No book is assigned to more than one student.
All books must be allocated.
The objective is to minimize the maximum number of pages assigned to any student. In other words, out of all possible allocations, 
find the arrangement where the student who receives the most pages still has the smallest possible maximum.
If it is not possible to allocate books to all students, return -1;

class Solution {
    long long maxallocation(vector<int> &arr,long long mid){
        // lets the the cnt to be 1 that obious reason
        long long cnt = 1;
        long long sum = 0;
        for(int i=0;i<arr.size();i++){
            // we will sum the pages if any moment it exceeds the mid value 
            // we will go to the else part where we increase the count
            // that means from there we have started givig books to new person
            // ans give him arr[i] number of book 
            if(sum+arr[i]<=mid){
                sum+=arr[i];
            }
            else{
                cnt++;
                sum=arr[i];
            }
        }
        
        return cnt;
    }
  public:
    int findPages(vector<int> &arr, int k) {
        // the binary search on answers
        // first make the range
        // low => max element why? because if you have to allocate books
        // among arr.size() element then obiously you can allocate a max 
        // of max_element page to a person 
        // and the high => max sum of all the elements in that array.
        
        long long low =  *max_element(arr.begin(),arr.end());
        long long high = accumulate(arr.begin(),arr.end(),0LL);
        
        
        // if you have this k greater than arr.size() thats is the case
        // to return -1.
        if(arr.size()<k) return -1;
        
        while(low<=high){
            
            long long mid = (high-low)/2+low;
            // now we are getting the books distributed among cnt people that can have max
            // mid pages in with them how if the number of pages is less and equal to k
            // that means we are at the right and we should move to the left.
            if(maxallocation(arr,mid)<=k){
                high = mid-1;
            }
            // that means we have a lot of people and we need to go to the right
            else low = mid+1;
        }
        return low;
    }
};
